Hello, I'm Zhao Chen 👋👋, a Master's student in Biomedical Engineering (BME) at ![CityU Logo](/icon/cityu.png) [City University of Hong Kong (CityU)](https://www.cityu.edu.hk/). 

My learning journey has been a bit **unconventional** 😂: Undergraduate background rooted in the interdisciplinary field of **Medical Informatics**; later developed a passion for **Computer Vision (CV)**, self-taught OpenCV, deep learning-based image detection/segmentation/human pose estimation, and attempted to solve few-shot segmentation problems; now fully immersed in the world of **Large Language Models (LLMs)**, exploring the intersection of natural language processing and biomedical engineering. For more details about my background, feel free to check my [resume](./resume.pdf). 

💻 **Recent Learning & Projects:** 
- Systematically organize the Agent development process, use the Qwen-Agent framework for rewriting, and complete the setup of the intelligent agent project module from 0 to 1; 
- Current projects:
  1. HopCandy: An observable Agentic RAG workbench for multi-hop question answering over financial annual reports; 
  2. Develop an Agent from scratch; 
  3. StarCore MedLink Smart Healthcare Platform; 
- Five completed projects:
  1. ChatBI Intelligent Data Analysis Assistant (Securities Research Scenario, Text2SQL, Time Series Forecasting, Dynamic Visualization); 
  2. General browser automation Agent (based on OpenManus MCP protocol, three-layer fallback positioning mechanism, long-link task success rate 80%); 
  3. Chinese medical large model LoRA fine-tuning (Qwen3.5-0.8B, BLEU 212.9%, VRAM only 1.43GB); 
  4. Enterprise RAG System (Intelligent Retrieval and Q&A for Internal Documents); 
  5. AI search applications (Elasticsearch rapid retrieval of massive data); 
- future exploration focus: The potential of **Small Language Models (SLMs)** and **Multimodal large model (Multimodal)** applications;
- detailed learning notes, reproduction codes, and more are available on my [GitHub](https://github.com/chenzhao-labs). 

🔍 **Career Goal:** To integrate my interdisciplinary background in medical-engineering and LLM expertise, exploring the practical applications of AI in healthcare, and becoming a cross-disciplinary engineer proficient in both healthcare and algorithms. 

🔬 **Research Interests:** Large Language Models (LLMs), Agent development, Medical AI, Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI)
